course: dictionary
lesson: 9237
title: Soothing words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To soothe someone is to make them calm when they are upset, angry or worried. To soothe pain is to make it feel less bad. «When a new baby arrives, parents spend hours feeding, changing and soothing it.» A baby that is crying is upset, so soothing it means calming it down.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «Cool water can soothe a sting» has no person in it, so the word is about pain: the sting hurts less. Ask yourself: what is being calmed, or made to feel less bad? Then swap in "calm" or "made less bad" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Soothe is a verb, so its form changes: soothe, soothes, soothed, soothing. «Soothing music» uses the -ing form to describe music that makes you feel calm and relaxed. Notice that the word can describe a thing as well as an action.
fact: Soothe is a verb: soothe, soothes, soothed, soothing.
fact: «Soothe» can mean to calm someone who is upset, angry or worried.
fact: «Soothe» can also mean to make pain feel less bad, as in «soothe the pain».
fact: «Soothing music» is music that makes you feel calm.
fact: In «Dock leaves on nettle stings help mostly because rubbing and coolness soothe», the sting feels less bad, but the leaf is not a strong cure.
exercise: «When a new baby arrives, parents spend hours feeding, changing and soothing it.» What does soothing mean here? | Waking it up for a big party | Dressing it in its best clothes | *Calming it down when it is upset | Making it cry louder
exercise: «Cool water can soothe a sting.» What is being made to feel less bad? | The water | The sun | *The sting | The leaf
exercise: What does «soothing music» mean? | Music that makes you feel calm | *Music that makes you feel calm and relaxed | Music that you cannot hear | Music that is very loud and fast
test: «Warm drinks and soup can soothe a sore throat.» What is being made to feel less bad? | The drinks | The soup | *The sore throat | The cold
test: «Parents soothed the crying child until it fell asleep.» What does soothed mean? | Hurt badly | Ignored completely | Forgotten at home | *Calmed when upset
exam: Which sentence uses soothe to mean calm someone who is upset? | «The sun is very bright today.» | «Cool water is refreshing on a hot day.» | *«Parents soothe a crying baby with rocking and singing.» | «Aloe vera soothes sunburn.»
